# Raw/Repair Dual Reporting v1

## Purpose
Prevent metric confusion by enforcing split reporting between model raw output and repair-layer output.

## Always
- Report both `raw` and `repair_v2` metrics together when discussing quality.
- Include explicit delta: `repair_v2_minus_raw`.
- Label repaired scores as `operational (post-processor included)`.
- Keep wording factual: avoid implying repaired score is base-model quality.

## Never
- Never collapse `raw` and `repair_v2` into a single "model score".
- Never claim Track A readiness from repair-only uplift.
- Never omit one side when citing a headline number.

## Required Output Block
- `raw`: parse_ok_rate, alignment_pass_rate, rows
- `repair_v2`: parse_ok_rate, alignment_pass_rate, repair_applied_count, rows
- `delta`: alignment_pass_rate_delta_repair_v2_minus_raw
